{"title":"Career Roadmap · Plant Manager (Dairy)","role":"Plant Manager (Dairy)","summary":"A Dairy Plant Manager oversees the complete operation of a dairy-processing facility, including milk reception, processing, quality, production, packaging, maintenance, utilities, food safety, supply chain, workforce and cost management.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Dairy Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Dairy Technology is directly aligned with this career because the degree combines dairy processing, food microbiology, chemistry, engineering, quality control and plant operations."},{"type":"note","label":"Career positioning","text":"Plant Manager is generally a mid-to-senior-career destination, not the typical first job after B.Tech. A graduate would normally begin as a Production Trainee, Dairy Technologist, Production Officer, Quality Officer or Process Engineer, then progress into supervisory and managerial positions."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Tech Dairy Technology"},{"text":"Dairy processing, food safety, production, quality"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Trainee / Production / Quality Officer"},{"text":"Plant operations and process control"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Production Manager / Assistant Plant Manager"},{"text":"Production, people, quality and cost"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Plant Manager / Operations Head"},{"text":"Complete plant performance and strategy"}]]}]},{"heading":"What a Dairy Plant Manager Does","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Plant Manager is responsible for coordinating:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Milk reception"},{"text":"Raw-milk testing"},{"text":"Pasteurisation"},{"text":"Homogenisation"},{"text":"Separation"},{